  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1991-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\[ \\sec^2\\theta=\\frac1{\\cos^2\\theta} =\\frac{\\csc^2\\theta}{\\csc^2\\theta-1}, \\] choose \\(x=\\csc^2\\theta\\) in the definition. Then \\[ f(\\sec^2\\theta)=\\frac1{\\csc^2\\theta}=\\sin^2\\theta. \\]\n\nThus the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Choose \\(x\\) so that \\(\\frac{1}{x}=\\sec^2\\theta\\)",
        "Use \\(1-\\cos^2\\theta=\\sin^2\\theta\\)"
      ],
